        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence from the Corpora section (c-2b39005de67979a14fc26cd7) directly describes the training data: parallel/versioned corpora pairing historical documents with their modern counterparts. Specifically, the Dutch Bible corpus uses the 1637 version as the original and the 1888 version as modern Dutch; El Quijote uses the 17th-century Spanish novel paired with its 21st-century version; El Conde Lucanor (14th-century with 21st-century version) was only used as test, and since no suitable training corpus was found, systems trained on El Quijote were used to modernize it. The Results section also notes the training corpora are small, a known problem for NMT. This fully answers what kind of data is used to train the model."
      },
